2. vendor/functions/: the detection kernel, copied verbatim
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Every file in vendor/functions/ is a byte-identical copy of the corresponding
file in functions/ of the author's STA/LTA package stalta_multichan_v1 (the
paper's STA/LTA baseline package, archived in the stalta_multichan_v1/ folder
of matched_filter_release.zip in the Zenodo record
https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.20715241; stalta_multichan_v1 is not published
as a separate GitHub repository because its detection functionality is included
here).
That directory mixes the author's own code with third-party code:

  2a. vendor/functions/readers.py, vendor/functions/stalta.py
      Written by Yuhan Wang (stalta_multichan_v1). MIT License,
      Copyright (c) 2026 Yuhan Wang.

  2b. Third-party code from ETH Zurich. NOT covered by the MIT License of
      this repository.

      vendor/functions/pydas_readers/
          readers/load_das_h5.py, readers/write_das_h5.py,
          util/block_cleaning.py, util/block_filters.py, util/block_spectra.py,
          mapping/channel_mapping.py
        "pydas_readers" by Daniel Bowden, ETH Zurich. He is named as the
        author in the headers of load_das_h5.py, write_das_h5.py and
        block_filters.py; the other files carry no author line and belong to
        the same package.

      vendor/functions/load_das_h5_PE2024.py
        By Pascal Edme, ETH Zurich. Its header states that it was "Derived
        from Sara and Daniel's original code to read Silixa iDASv2 format",
        i.e. earlier reader code by Sara Klaasen and Daniel Bowden
        (ETH Zurich).

      Status of the files listed in 2b:
        - No license text was distributed with these files, and no public
          upstream release (PyPI or GitHub) was found. All rights remain with
          their authors.
        - They are redistributed here without changes (byte-identical to the
          copies in stalta_multichan_v1/functions/), for research and
          reproducibility, with the permission of the authors (Daniel Bowden,
          Pascal Edme and Sara Klaasen). Please contact the original authors
          before reusing these files outside this repository.
        - The only change made here: the three channel-mapping CSV files that
          originally came with vendor/functions/pydas_readers/mapping/ (a
          channel map from another, unrelated project) were removed.
          channel_mapping.py itself is unchanged; this application never
          calls it, and its get_mapping() would need such a CSV file.


